    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1091416">NP 0F F4 /r<superscript><footnote><para unique="1091412" format="TableFootnote">See note in <link unique="1091410" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#27214: 02_Level: 2.4 Instruction Exception Specification" xrefstyle="SectionNum&amp;Title(,)">Section 2.5, &#8220;Intel&#174; AVX and Intel&#174; SSE Instruction Exception Classification,&#8221;</link> in the Intel&#174; 64 and IA&#8209;32 Architectures Soft&#173;ware Developer&#8217;s Manual, Volume 2A, and <link unique="1092437" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol3B_ch25.fm#65163: 03_Level: 19.25.3 Exception Conditions of Legacy SIMD Instruction Operating" xrefstyle="SectionNum&amp;Title(,)">Section 25.25.3, &#8220;Exception Conditions of Legacy SIMD Instructions Operating on MMX Registers,&#8221;</link> in the Intel&#174; 64 and IA&#8209;32 Architectures Software Developer&#8217;s Manual, Volume 3B.</para>
         </footnote></superscript></para>
      <para unique="1091417">PMULUDQ mm1, mm2/m64</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091421">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091423">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091425">SSE2</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091427">Multiply unsigned doubleword integer in mm1 by unsigned doubleword integer in mm2/m64, and store the quadword result in mm1. </para>
      </td>
